  "estimatedMinutes": 1,
  "statement": "A football game was played between two teams, the Cougars and the Panthers. The two teams scored a total of \\(34\\) points, and the Cougars won by a margin of \\(14\\) points. How many points did the Panthers score?",
  "answerChoices": [
    {
      "label": "A",
      "text": "\\(10\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "B",
      "text": "\\(14\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "C",
      "text": "\\(17\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "D",
      "text": "\\(20\\)"
    },
    {
      "label": "E",
      "text": "\\(24\\)"
    }
  ],
  "answer": {
    "letter": "a",
    "value": "10"
  },
  "solutions": [
    {
      "id": "sol.amc-10b-2006-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Let \\(c\\) and \\(p\\) be the Cougars’ and Panthers’ scores. Then \\(c+p=34\\) and \\(c-p=14.\\) Subtracting gives \\(2p=20,\\) so \\(p=10.\\)\n\nThus, the correct answer is A.",
      "hints": [
        "Let the two scores be \\(c\\) and \\(p\\) with \\(c+p=34\\)",
        "The winning margin gives \\(c-p=14\\)"
      ],
